erivation.md\\n+++ b/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/02-message-level-derivation.md\\n@@ -148,6 +148,12 @@ Risk Reminders:\\n | Date | Deviation | Disposition |\\n |---|---|---|\\n | 2026-06-10 | Sanctioned Epic 01 test amendments (F-03 patch, test plan §Sanctioned Amendments): `tool_call` now queues `tool_call_summary`, so `test/work-queue.test.ts` exact-count assertions go 3→4 work rows (`messageWork` 2→3); red manifest regenerated as an explicit story step. No other Epic 01 edits sanctioned | Planned amendment; record actual edits here during implementation |\\n+| 2026-06-11 | Actual sanctioned-amendment edits (the planned tool_call sweep): `test/work-queue.test.ts` restart-survival rows 3→4 (`messageWork` 2→3, list gains `w-m2-tool_call_summary-v1`) + TC-2.9 kind-gate comment; `test/work-execution.test.ts` TC-1.1 (4 items, 5 forms) and maxItems leg (remaining 2→3); `test/cli-process-work.test.ts` TC-1.3 (4 seeded items, 3-row after-kill detail, 5 final forms) — the latter two are Epic 02 Story 0/1 files caught by the same sweep rule. Red manifest regenerated for all three plus the new suite | Implemented; behavior-preserving count/id updates only |\\n+| 2026-06-11 | `test/work-queue.test.ts` handler-map assembly test (Story 0) amended: `expect(sdk.workHandlers).toEqual({})` cannot survive Story 2 registering the real messages table — now asserts exactly the three message kinds and probes the miss with `turn_derivation` (unregistered until Story 3) | Necessary consequence of the story's registration step, not in the pre-listed sweep; flagged for verifier attention |\\n+| 2026-06-11 | Intake touch sites live in `src/domains/messages/index.ts`, not `intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts` as the design table says: Epic 01 placed `MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS` and the per-message queue step in the messages domain (pipeline already calls `queueMessageWork` per recorded event). Both touches (kind-map addition; late-result lookup keyed by the projected `toolCallId`) ride the same batch transaction the design requires; `pipeline.ts` needed no edit | Same semantics, owning-domain placement |\\n+| 2026-06-11 | Call-id pairing index `idx_message_block_tool_call_id` added to `MIGRATION_V5_STATEMENTS` in place (anti-shim: the AC-2.8 lookup and the handlers' paired reads must be one indexed query, never a scan). v5 is amended rather than a v6 appended because the tech design pins \\\"one migration for the epic\\\" and `thread-migration.test.ts` asserts version 5; a file already migrated to v5 before this story keeps working (queries fall back to a scan, correctness unaffected) — a non-issue pre-release | Schema addition inside the epic's single migration |\\n+| 2026-06-11 | `tool_result_summary` forms also carry `metadata.outcome` (stamped from the result's own `isError` via `outcome.ts`) — the epic's tool-activity outcome contract and the Story 0 multi-state fixture already claim this shape; the story text names only the call summary | Additive, consistent with AC-2.4's mechanism |\\n+| 2026-06-11 | \\\"Form read-back on message reads\\\" (Implementation Targets, Surface row) not added to `listMessages`: no TC in this story consumes it (the test plan reads forms directly via the fixture reader) and the per-owner report join is Story 4's deliverable | Deferred to Story 4's report surface |\\n \\n ### Definition of Done\\n <!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:91:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_43\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts | sed -n '1,220p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t// The three message-level derivation handlers (Flow 2): prompt smoothing,\\n     2\\t// tool-call summary, tool-result summary. One shape throughout — read the\\n     3\\t// source message (a tool-activity handler additionally joins its call-id\\n     4\\t// pair, nothing more: AC-2.5), call exactly one provider operation, hand the\\n     5\\t// form content back through HandlerOutcome. The drain's completion\\n     6\\t// transaction performs the version-checked UPDATE-only write (Story 1), so a\\n     7\\t// stale or deleted source discards here exactly as everywhere else. Outcomes\\n     8\\t// on tool-activity summaries come from outcome.ts — the record, never the\\n     9\\t// provider's text (AC-2.4) — and land in form metadata apart from content.\\n    10\\timport type {\\n    11\\t  HandlerFormWrite,\\n    12\\t  HandlerOutcome,\\n    13\\t  HandlerRunContext,\\n    14\\t  WorkHandler,\\n    15\\t} from \\\"../../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n    16\\timport type { WorkKind } from \\\"../../../tech-utils/work-queue/index.js\\\";\\n    17\\timport { deriveToolOutcome } from \\\"./outcome.js\\\";\\n    18\\timport {\\n    19\\t  findPairedToolCall,\\n    20\\t  findPairedToolResult,\\n    21\\t  readMessageSource,\\n    22\\t  type MessageSource,\\n    23\\t} from \\\"./forms.js\\\";\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\t// A handler that cannot read its source coherently has found source damage:\\n    26\\t// terminal, form blocked with the reason (never a retry loop against a\\n    27\\t// record that cannot improve). A *deleted* source never reaches this — its\\n    28\\t// form row is gone and the completion write would discard — so a miss here\\n    29\\t// is genuine corruption.\\n    30\\tfunction sourceDamaged(reason: string): HandlerOutcome {\\n    31\\t  return { ok: false, blocked: true, reason: `source_damaged: ${reason}` };\\n    32\\t}\\n    33\\t\\n    34\\tfunction loadSource(\\n    35\\t  run: HandlerRunContext,\\n    36\\t  item: { sourceRef: Record<string, string> },\\n    37\\t  expectedKind: string,\\n    38\\t):\\n    39\\t  | { ok: true; messageId: string; source: MessageSource }\\n    40\\t  | { ok: false; outcome: HandlerOutcome } {\\n    41\\t  const messageId = item.sourceRef[\\\"messageId\\\"];\\n    42\\t  if (messageId === undefined) {\\n    43\\t    return { ok: false, outcome: sourceDamaged(\\\"work item carries no messageId\\\") };\\n    44\\t  }\\n    45\\t  const source = readMessageSource(run.openDb(), messageId);\\n    46\\t  if (source === undefined) {\\n    47\\t    return { ok: false, outcome: sourceDamaged(`message ${messageId} not found`) };\\n    48\\t  }\\n    49\\t  if (source.kind !== expectedKind) {\\n    50\\t    return {\\n    51\\t      ok: false,\\n    52\\t      outcome: sourceDamaged(\\n    53\\t        `message ${messageId} is kind ${source.kind}, expected ${expectedKind}`,\\n    54\\t      ),\\n    55\\t    };\\n    56\\t  }\\n    57\\t  return { ok: true, messageId, source };\\n    58\\t}\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\tfunction landForm(\\n    61\\t  write: HandlerFormWrite,\\n    62\\t  result: { ok: true; text: string } | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string },\\n    63\\t): HandlerOutcome {\\n    64\\t  if (!result.ok) return { ok: false, retryable: result.retryable, reason: result.reason };\\n    65\\t  return { ok: true, forms: [{ ...write, content: result.text }] };\\n    66\\t}\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tconst smoothPromptHandler: WorkHandler = async (run, item) => {\\n    69\\t  const loaded = loadSource(run, item, \\\"user_prompt\\\");\\n    70\\t  if (!loaded.ok) return loaded.outcome;\\n    71\\t  const text = loaded.source.blocks[0]?.content[\\\"text\\\"];\\n    72\\t  if (typeof text !== \\\"string\\\") {\\n    73\\t    return sourceDamaged(`prompt ${loaded.messageId} has no text block`);\\n    74\\t  }\\n    75\\t  return landForm(\\n    76\\t    {\\n    77\\t      subjectKind: \\\"message\\\",\\n    78\\t      subjectId: loaded.messageId,\\n    79\\t      form: \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\",\\n    80\\t      content: \\\"\\\",\\n    81\\t    },\\n    82\\t    await run.provider.smoothPrompt({ text }),\\n    83\\t  );\\n    84\\t};\\n    85\\t\\n    86\\tconst toolCallSummaryHandler: WorkHandler = async (run, item) => {\\n    87\\t  const loaded = loadSource(run, item, \\\"tool_call\\\");\\n    88\\t  if (!loaded.ok) return loaded.outcome;\\n    89\\t  const block = loaded.source.blocks[0]?.content ?? {};\\n    90\\t  const toolCallId = block[\\\"toolCallId\\\"];\\n    91\\t  const toolName = block[\\\"toolName\\\"];\\n    92\\t  if (typeof toolCallId !== \\\"string\\\" || typeof toolName !== \\\"string\\\") {\\n    93\\t    return sourceDamaged(`tool call ${loaded.messageId} has no tool_call block`);\\n    94\\t  }\\n    95\\t  // The handler's one reach beyond its message: the paired result by call id\\n    96\\t  // (AC-2.5). Outcome is stamped from that pairing mechanically — present and\\n    97\\t  // clean, present and isError, or absent — before the provider ever runs.\\n    98\\t  const paired = findPairedToolResult(run.openDb(), toolCallId);\\n    99\\t  const outcome = deriveToolOutcome(paired);\\n   100\\t  const input: Parameters<typeof run.provider.summarizeToolCall>[0] = {\\n   101\\t    toolName,\\n   102\\t    argsJson: JSON.stringify(block[\\\"arguments\\\"] ?? {}),\\n   103\\t  };\\n   104\\t  if (paired !== undefined) {\\n   105\\t    input.pairedResult = { content: paired.content, isError: paired.isError };\\n   106\\t  }\\n   107\\t  return landForm(\\n   108\\t    {\\n   109\\t      subjectKind: \\\"message\\\",\\n   110\\t      subjectId: loaded.messageId,\\n   111\\t      form: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n   112\\t      content: \\\"\\\",\\n   113\\t      metadata: { outcome },\\n   114\\t    },\\n   115\\t    await run.provider.summarizeToolCall(input),\\n   116\\t  );\\n   117\\t};\\n   118\\t\\n   119\\tconst toolResultSummaryHandler: WorkHandler = async (run, item) => {\\n   120\\t  const loaded = loadSource(run, item, \\\"tool_result\\\");\\n   121\\t  if (!loaded.ok) return loaded.outcome;\\n   122\\t  const block = loaded.source.blocks[0]?.content ?? {};\\n   123\\t  const content = block[\\\"content\\\"];\\n   124\\t  if (typeof content !== \\\"string\\\") {\\n   125\\t    return sourceDamaged(`tool result ${loaded.messageId} has no tool_result block`);\\n   126\\t  }\\n   127\\t  const toolCallId = block[\\\"toolCallId\\\"];\\n   128\\t  const pairedCall =\\n   129\\t    typeof toolCallId === \\\"string\\\"\\n   130\\t      ? findPairedToolCall(run.openDb(), toolCallId)\\n   131\\t      : undefined;\\n   132\\t  // The summary abbreviates; the full result content stays untouched in the\\n   133\\t  // record (AC-2.3) — nothing here writes back to message_block. The result\\n   134\\t  // is tool activity, so its outcome is stamped from its own isError flag.\\n   135\\t  return landForm(\\n   136\\t    {\\n   137\\t      subjectKind: \\\"message\\\",\\n   138\\t      subjectId: loaded.messageId,\\n   139\\t      form: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n   140\\t      content: \\\"\\\",\\n   141\\t      metadata: { outcome: deriveToolOutcome({ isError: block[\\\"isError\\\"] === true }) },\\n   142\\t    },\\n   143\\t    await run.provider.summarizeToolResult({\\n   144\\t      toolName: pairedCall?.toolName ?? \\\"unknown_tool\\\",\\n   145\\t      content,\\n   146\\t    }),\\n   147\\t  );\\n   148\\t};\\n   149\\t\\n   150\\t// The domain's handler table, merged into the SDK dispatch map at\\n   151\\t// construction (DD-6). Turn-owned kinds stay with the turns domain.\\n   152\\texport const messageWorkHandlers: Readonly<Partial<Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>>> = {\\n   153\\t  prompt_smoothing: smoothPromptHandler,\\n   154\\t  tool_call_summary: toolCallSummaryHandler,\\n   155\\t  tool_result_summary: toolResultSummaryHandler,\\n   156\\t};\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:92:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_44\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts | sed -n '70,170p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    70\\t  insertMessage(ctx.db, {\\n    71\\t    messageId,\\n    72\\t    sourceEventOrder: event.eventOrder,\\n    73\\t    kind,\\n    74\\t    tokenEstimate: projected.tokenEstimate,\\n    75\\t    actor: event.actor,\\n    76\\t    harness: event.harness,\\n    77\\t    turnId,\\n    78\\t    blocks: projected.blocks,\\n    79\\t  });\\n    80\\t  if (event.eventKind === \\\"tool_call\\\" || event.eventKind === \\\"tool_result\\\") {\\n    81\\t    return { messageId, kind, toolCallId: event.payload.toolCallId };\\n    82\\t  }\\n    83\\t  return { messageId, kind };\\n    84\\t}\\n    85\\t\\n    86\\t// The kind gate, exact by design: a prompt queues prompt_smoothing, a tool\\n    87\\t// call queues tool_call_summary (Epic 02 Story 2's additive extension), a\\n    88\\t// tool result queues tool_result_summary, nothing else queues anything —\\n    89\\t// text, thinking, and note messages are not derivation sources (Epic 01\\n    90\\t// AC-2.8/TC-2.9; Epic 02 AC-2.2/AC-2.7). Cross-domain surface, called by\\n    91\\t// intake-stream inside the batch transaction for every recorded message, so\\n    92\\t// the item commits (or rolls back) with the batch.\\n    93\\tconst MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS: Partial<Record<EventKind, WorkKind>> = {\\n    94\\t  user_prompt: \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n    95\\t  tool_call: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n    96\\t  tool_result: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n    97\\t};\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\t// Which derived form each message-owned kind produces — the owning domain's\\n   100\\t// knowledge, handed to the meaning-blind enqueue so the form's pending row\\n   101\\t// rides the same transaction (DD-5).\\n   102\\tconst MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS: Partial<Record<WorkKind, FormKind>> = {\\n   103\\t  prompt_smoothing: \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\",\\n   104\\t  tool_call_summary: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n   105\\t  tool_result_summary: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n   106\\t};\\n   107\\t\\n   108\\t// Message-owned work handlers, merged into the SDK's dispatch map at\\n   109\\t// construction (DD-6): prompt smoothing and the two tool-activity summaries.\\n   110\\texport const workHandlers: Readonly<Partial<Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>>> =\\n   111\\t  messageWorkHandlers;\\n   112\\t\\n   113\\texport function queueMessageWork(\\n   114\\t  ctx: OperationContext,\\n   115\\t  message: MessageCreated,\\n   116\\t): WorkItemRecord[] {\\n   117\\t  if (message === null) return [];\\n   118\\t  const items: WorkItemRecord[] = [];\\n   119\\t  const kind = MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS[message.kind];\\n   120\\t  if (kind !== undefined) {\\n   121\\t    const form = MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS[kind];\\n   122\\t    if (form === undefined) {\\n   123\\t      // Every queuing kind names its form above; a miss is a wiring bug.\\n   124\\t      throw new Error(`no derived form mapped for message work kind ${kind}`);\\n   125\\t    }\\n   126\\t    items.push(\\n   127\\t      enqueue(ctx, {\\n   128\\t        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n   129\\t        kind,\\n   130\\t        sourceRef: { messageId: message.messageId },\\n   131\\t        forms: [{ subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: message.messageId, form }],\\n   132\\t      }),\\n   133\\t    );\\n   134\\t  }\\n   135\\t  // Late-result repair (AC-2.8): a tool result landing after its call's\\n   136\\t  // summary already derived with outcome \\\"unknown\\\" means the summary's\\n   137\\t  // source — the call+result pair — completed underneath it; clear and\\n   138\\t  // regenerate at the next source version, in this same batch transaction.\\n   139\\t  // One indexed lookup; pending summaries (metadata NULL) never match, so\\n   140\\t  // the common call-and-result-in-one-batch case never triggers, and the\\n   141\\t  // version-scoped item id keeps the requeue idempotent.\\n   142\\t  if (message.kind === \\\"tool_result\\\" && message.toolCallId !== undefined) {\\n   143\\t    const stale = findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary(ctx.db, message.toolCallId);\\n   144\\t    if (stale !== undefined) {\\n   145\\t      items.push(\\n   146\\t        enqueue(ctx, {\\n   147\\t          owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n   148\\t          kind: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n   149\\t          sourceRef: { messageId: stale.messageId },\\n   150\\t          sourceVersion: stale.sourceVersion + 1,\\n   151\\t          forms: [\\n   152\\t            {\\n   153\\t              subjectKind: \\\"message\\\",\\n   154\\t              subjectId: stale.messageId,\\n   155\\t              form: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n   156\\t            },\\n   157\\t          ],\\n   158\\t        }),\\n   159\\t      );\\n   160\\t    }\\n   161\\t  }\\n   162\\t  return items;\\n   163\\t}\\n   164\\t\\n   165\\tfunction threadNotFound(filePath: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n   166\\t  return {\\n   167\\t    ok: false,\\n   168\\t    error: {\\n   169\\t      errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   170\\t      code: \\\"thread_not_found\\\",\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:93:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_45\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \\\"tool_result|tool_call|toolCallId|isError|arguments|toolName\\\" packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/validate.ts packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/project.ts packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:94:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_46\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \\\"fake|mock|shim|placeholder|TODO|n