{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/02-message-level-derivation.md | sed -n '28,86p'\"","aggregated_output":"    28\t### Acceptance Criteria\n    29\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\n    30\t\n    31\t- **AC-2.1**: A user prompt message's smoothing work, when run, lands a smoothed form in `ready` state, readable alongside the message.\n    32\t  - **TC-2.1** (AC-2.1): Intake a prompt, drain → smoothed form `ready`, content is the double's deterministic output for that input.\n    33\t- **AC-2.2**: A tool-call message's summary work lands a summary naming the tool and describing its arguments, with an outcome field; a `tool_call` event in an intake batch queues a `tool_call_summary` work item the same way Epic 01 queues the other message-level kinds — an additive extension of the Epic 01 intake path that stays deterministic and local.\n    34\t  - **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2): Intake a `tool_call` event → batch result reports a `tool_call_summary` work item queued, intake result returned before any handler ran; drain → summary `ready`, names the tool, describes the arguments.\n    35\t- **AC-2.3**: A tool-result message's summary work lands a summarized abbreviation in `ready` state; the full result content remains untouched in the record.\n    36\t  - **TC-2.3** (AC-2.3): Intake a tool call and large result, drain → result summary `ready`; full content reads back byte-identical to intake.\n    37\t- **AC-2.4**: A tool-activity summary's outcome is stamped from the record: result present with `isError: false` → succeeded; `isError: true` → failed; no paired result → unknown. The provider's text never determines the outcome field.\n    38\t  - **TC-2.4** (AC-2.4): Three intake variants — result ok, result `isError`, call with no result → outcomes succeeded, failed, unknown; double's text identical across all three, proving text doesn't drive outcome.\n    39\t- **AC-2.5**: Message-level derivation reads only the message and its call-id-paired counterpart; no turn or chunk context is an input.\n    40\t  - **TC-2.5** (AC-2.5): Double records its inputs → tool-call summary input contains the call and paired result only; no turn data.\n    41\t- **AC-2.6**: A provider failure on a message-level item follows Flow 1 retry policy; exhaustion lands the form `failed` with the provider's reason, and the message itself remains fully readable.\n    42\t  - **TC-2.6** (AC-2.6): Double exhausts retries on smoothing → form `failed` with reason; message read-back unaffected.\n    43\t- **AC-2.7**: Message kinds with no derivable form (assistant text, thinking, runtime notes) queue no message-level work and carry no derivation state rows.\n    44\t  - **TC-2.7** (AC-2.7): Intake assistant text and a runtime note, drain → no work items for them, no derivation state rows on read-back.\n    45\t- **AC-2.8**: A tool result arriving after its call's summary already landed with outcome `unknown` re-queues that summary at intake: the pair is the summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate like any source change. The check is deterministic and local (one indexed lookup by call id); the common case — call and result in one batch — never triggers it, because the summary runs after both landed.\n    46\t  - **TC-2.8** (AC-2.8): Intake a `tool_call` alone, drain (summary lands `unknown`), then intake its `tool_result` in a later batch → summary work re-queued at intake; drain → outcome now `succeeded`, one summary form, no duplicates. Control: call and result in one batch → no re-queue ever fires.\n    47\t\n    48\t### Technical Design\n    49\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\n    50\t\n    51\t#### Architecture Context\n    52\t\n    53\tFirst real handlers through Story 1's drain — and the proof that the handler-map seam carries domain behavior. All three live in `messages/internal/handlers.ts`, follow one shape (read source → call one provider op → land form via `forms.ts` UPDATE-only write with source-version check — the pending row exists from enqueue), and stay message-local: the tool-call handler's only reach is the paired result by `tool_call_id`, through `outcome.ts`, which derives `succeeded | failed | unknown` from `isError`/presence — mechanically, never from provider text (AC-2.4 is this epic's receipts principle in code).\n    54\t\n    55\tThe story touches intake twice, both deterministic and local (NFR: no inference on the hot path): `MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS` gains `tool_call: \"tool_call_summary\"`, and projecting a `tool_result` does one indexed lookup — paired call's summary with `metadata.outcome = \"unknown\"` → requeue in the batch transaction (AC-2.8). The requeue rides Story 1's enqueue (dedupe makes it idempotent); the common single-batch case never fires it because the summary hasn't run yet when the result lands.\n    56\t\n    57\t#### Build Strategy\n    58\t\n    59\tStrategy: tdd-lite\n    60\t\n    61\tReason:\n    62\t- Handler logic is straightforward, but two behaviors invite shortcuts: outcome could silently come from text patterns (passes TC-2.1–2.3, violates the design's core rule), and the late-result requeue could be approximated with a re-derive-on-read hack. Red tests for TC-2.4 and TC-2.8 pin both before implementation.\n    63\t\n    64\tRisk Reminders:\n    65\t- TC-2.4's three variants use *identical double text* — that's what proves text-independence; don't weaken the fixture.\n    66\t- TC-2.8's control leg (call+result same batch → no re-queue) is half the AC; the capture log proves the summary ran once.\n    67\t- Intake-return-before-handler (TC-2.2) asserts the double's capture log is empty at intake return — the no-inference-on-hot-path NFR made testable.\n    68\t\n    69\t#### Implementation Targets\n    70\t\n    71\t| Area | Files / Modules |\n    72\t|------|-----------------|\n    73\t| Handlers | `src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts` (NEW: three handlers, registered in `messages.workHandlers`) |\n    74\t| Outcome | `src/domains/messages/internal/outcome.ts` (NEW: mechanical derivation, pure function) |\n    75\t| Form storage | `src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts` (NEW: UPDATE-only writes with source-version check; read joins) |\n    76\t| Intake touch 1 | `src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts` (`MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS` + tool_call) |\n    77\t| Intake touch 2 | same file, tool_result projection step (unknown-outcome lookup → requeue) |\n    78\t| Surface | `src/domains/messages/index.ts` (workHandlers export; form read-back on message reads) |\n    79\t| Tests | `test/derivation-messages.test.ts` (NEW) |\n    80\t\n    81\t#### Design References\n    82\t\n    83\t- [tech-design.md §Flow 2 (handler mechanics, both intake touches)](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md:225), lines 225–226\n    84\t- [tech-design.md DD-2 (derived_form table), DD-3 (source-version stale-result check)](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md:75), lines 75–77\n    85\t- [tech-design.md §Storage (derived_form table, metadata column)](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md:155), lines 155–167\n    86\t- [tech-design.md §Interfaces (DerivedForm, ToolOutcome, provider ops 1–3)](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md:240), lines 240–282\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
